cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Pirate Pain — Multivariate Time-Series Classification"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zanoni
    given-names: Alessandro
  - family-names: Valentini
    given-names: Jacopo
  - family-names: Balducci
    given-names: Arianna
  - family-names: Gallicola
    given-names: Renato
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-11-17"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Solution to the first challenge of the Artificial Neural Networks and Deep
  Learning course (Politecnico di Milano, A.Y. 2025/26): classifying the pain
  level of a subject from 160 time steps of body-joint kinematics. The final
  model is a CMA-ES-weighted ensemble of two CNN-GRU networks operating at
  different temporal scales plus an InceptionTime network trained on an
  enriched feature representation, refined by a confidence-gated binary
  classifier. All networks are trained from scratch.
keywords:
  - time series classification
  - deep learning
  - ensemble methods
  - PyTorch
